  "facts": [
    "The Mælefjell Tunnel, Norway's seventh longest road tunnel, stretches 9.35 kilometres, cutting the E134 route by about 10 kilometres and shaving 18 minutes off truck journeys between Århus and Gvammen.",
    "Construction of the Mælefjell Tunnel began in 2013, with the breakthrough achieved on 3 May 2017, and the tunnel officially opened on 19 December 2019 after a 2 billion kr investment.",
    "By bypassing the hazardous Åsebrekken pass, the Mælefjell Tunnel dramatically improves safety and accessibility for heavy vehicles, replacing 22.6 kilometres of the old Flatdal road with 11.7 kilometres of new, smoother pavement."
  ],
